The jump from a $(2.3) billion loss in 2024 to a **$15.2 billion** gain in 2025 (a **$17.5 billion** improvement) was driven mainly by Anthropic-related valuation and conversion gains.  

Key contributors (all amounts per the 2025 10‑K):  
- **~$7.7 billion** upward fair‑value adjustments on Anthropic nonvoting preferred stock;  
- **~$5.6 billion** reclassification gains from Anthropic convertible notes converted to nonvoting preferred stock;  
- Marketable equity and warrant valuation gains (primarily **Rivian** and warrants) — **$1.4 billion** and **$553 million**, respectively;  
- Minor items: foreign currency **+$19 million** and other net **–$414 million**.  

In short, Anthropic fair‑value/conversion events were the primary driver, supplemented by public equity/warrant gains.
